LeetCode 863 – All Nodes Distance K in Binary Tree 
-Approach:
This problem requires treating the binary tree like an undirected graph, because from a node we can move:
Left child
Right child
Parent
I first built a parent map using DFS. Then I used BFS starting from the target node and explored the tree level by level until reaching distance K.
A HashSet keeps track of visited nodes so we don't traverse back and forth.

Time: O(n)
Space: O(n)
-Key Takeaways:
A tree can be converted into a graph-like structure using a parent map.
BFS is ideal for finding nodes at an exact distance.
The visited set prevents cycles when moving between child and parent.

